#: action.py:156
msgid "A comma-separated values (CSV) file is a delimited text file that uses a comma to separate values. A CSV file stores tabular data in plain text. Each line of the file is a data rows. Each rows consists of one or more values, separated by commas. The use of the comma as a value separator is the source of the name for this file format."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:160
msgid "Due to the lack of a strict CSV specification, different applications produce subtly different CSV file, but this plugin can tolerate some of such difference as input."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:162
msgid "The CSV format prefered by the plugin is the following:"
msgstr ""

#: action.py:164
msgid "The entire file must be saved in the Unicode (UTF-8) encoding."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:165
msgid "The value delimiter (column separator) must be a single comma (not tab-separated or fixed width)."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:166
msgid "The CSV require at least two columns."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:167
msgid "The CSV require at least two rows/lines:"
msgstr ""

#: action.py:168
msgid "The first row must be a \"header\" row which contains the double-quoted textual name of each column."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:169
msgid "All rows after the first row must contain either textual values or empty within each and every column."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:170
msgid "All rows must have the same number of double-quoted textual columns as the \"header\" row."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:172
msgid "All values should preferably be double-quoted."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:173
msgid "To include a double-quote character inside a value, write two double-quote consecutively <code>\"\"</code>."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:175
msgid "Is possible to insert a new line inside a double-quoted value, however not all software supports it properly. This plugin do."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:177
msgid "Leading and trailing spaces will be removed from each value automatically."
msgstr ""

#: action.py:178
